 "notModeled": [
  "analog input (pseudo-differential +IN/-IN, 0 V to VREF), internal 2.5-V reference and reference buffer",
  "the conversion starts at the CONVST falling edge only while CS is low, or at the CS falling edge while CONVST is low (Figures 1-2); the model starts it at every CONVST falling edge regardless of CS, and a CS fall does not start one",
  "sampling start rules (CONVST rising / CS falling / internal conversion end, Figure 3) and back-to-back operation timing (Figures 7-8): acquisition is not modeled",
  "conversion abort: CS falling while BUSY and CONVST are high aborts the conversion and the bus shows FE0h (Figure 4)",
  "PWD/RST: a low pulse of 45 ns to 6.14 us resets the device and a low level longer than 7.2 us powers it down; during the reset phase the bus reads FE0h; the first four conversions after power-up or reset are invalid; the 25-ms power-up delay; the model treats PWD/RST low as power-down only",
  "nap mode (A_PWD low): power saving between conversions, no digital effect except the 60-ns longer acquisition; the pin is an input only",
  "conversion time 280 ns max at +VBD = 5 V and 3 V (p.3, p.5); the model uses the maximum at +VBD = 3 V",
  "quiet-time requirements around the CONVST falling edge; data read during a conversion returns the previous result on the part (the model returns the 0 V code)",
  "BUSY rising delay td2 (40 ns) and falling delay td11 (20 ns) after the conversion",
  "byte mode: with BYTE high the bus shows D3-D0 on DB11-DB8 followed by zeros (Table 2); the model applies BYTE to every read"
 ],
